# Trivy ignore file — known/accepted vulnerabilities
# Each entry documents a specific CVE that is accepted as low-risk
# for this application's threat model.
#
# Format (Trivy 0.55+):
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXX [optional: reason]
#
# See docs/security-notes.md for rationale on each accepted risk.

# ── Accepted: Python stdlib unicode security issues ──────────────────
# These affect the Python interpreter itself, not application code.
# They require local code execution to exploit, which is outside our
# threat model.  Keep track for future Python version upgrades.

# ── Accepted: urllib3 / httpx related CVEs ───────────────────────────
# These affect the underlying HTTP transport, which is behind the
# FastAPI application layer.  Exploitation requires MITM position.
# Our API uses TLS in production.

# ── Accepted: Pillow / image processing ─────────────────────────────
# The app only handles PDF, DOCX, TXT files — not arbitrary image uploads.
# The PDF→image conversion (pdf2image) is only used for OCR fallback.
